        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Alan Furst, H. P. Lovecraft, Eric Ambler, Graham Greene, Joseph Roth, Arthur Koestler\n- Roles: American authors\n- Topics: Historical spy novels, horror fiction, literary influences, posthumous fame\n\nFacts:\n- H. P. Lovecraft was born on August 20, 1890, and died on March 15, 1937.\n- H. P. Lovecraft was an American author whose horror fiction became influential and brought him posthumous fame.\n- Alan Furst was born on February 20, 1941.\n- Alan Furst is an American author of historical spy novels.\n- Alan Furst has been called an heir to the tradition of Eric Ambler and Graham Greene.\n- Alan Furst cited Eric Ambler, Graham Greene, Joseph Roth, and Arthur Koestler as important influences.",
